WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Push a door right next to
its hinges, where it turns.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.490
It barely moves.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.850
Now push just as hard at
the handle, out at the edge,

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.350
far from the hinges.

5
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.950
It swings open.

6
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.390
Same push, different result.

7
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.490
So why does where you
push matter so much?

8
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.330
In this mission, you'll meet
a new idea about forces,

9
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.230
called a moment.

10
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.870
Then you'll explore pressure:
why a sharp knife cuts,

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.330
why water pushes harder
the deeper you go,

12
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.830
and why some things
float while others sink.

13
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.630
Your mission: explain why a door
handle is never next to the

14
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.740
hinges.
